    "result": "`check_password` is implemented in `solution.py`, following all six rules in `spec.md`. I wrote 8 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` and they pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nThe tests cover the type errors and the 12 and 64 length boundaries. They also cover each character class, the username rule (including names shorter than 3 characters), repeats, and blocklist equality, plus the order of the returned codes.\n\nI haven't seen results for the coverage, CRAP score, mutation or bandit gates, and I didn't run them. I split the logic into small helper functions to keep each one's complexity low. The test suite exercises every branch, so I expect coverage to be high, but that is untested.\n\nMy first run had one failing test, and the mistake was in the test. `é` and `!` are both \"other\" characters, so that password has only two classes. I corrected the expectation, not the implementation.",
